# netsurf: webkitAppearance JS binding + vendor-prefix name mapping (185 follow-up)
# Generated 2026-10-01
#
# Patch 185 answered getComputedStyle(el).appearance but not the prefixed
# name that webkit-flavoured pages probe:
#
# 1. qjs_get_computed_style now sets "webkitAppearance" alongside
#    "appearance" (same none/auto clamping). The vgcs Proxy in
#    vita_polyfill.js already maps getPropertyValue('-webkit-appearance')
#    -> camel('-webkit-appearance') = 'webkitAppearance' via its
#    prefix-aware camel(), so the native side just needed the property
#    present. Direct gcs.webkitAppearance also works through the proxy.
#
# 2. The element.style proxy (mk in macsurf_qjs.c) gains 'webkitAppearance'
#    in its PS property list, so el.style.webkitAppearance get/set works.
#
# 3. The proxy's name-mapping helpers are fixed for vendor prefixes:
#    cc('webkitAppearance') was 'webkit-appearance' (missing leading
#    dash); now '-webkit-appearance'. gu('-webkit-appearance') was
#    'WebkitAppearance' (capital W, missed the property); now
#    'webkitAppearance'. The fixes are prefix-scoped
#    (/^(webkit|moz|ms)-/ and /^-(webkit|moz|ms)-/) so non-prefixed
#    properties map exactly as before.
#
# Measurements: el.style.webkitAppearance round-trips; GCS answers both
# names; getPropertyValue('-webkit-appearance') hits.
# Decline conditions: none -- pure JS binding additions; no C control flow
# changes. If a page never touches the prefixed name, nothing executes.
